    <DataNode elementId="AT4G02280-MONOMER" textLabel="Sucrose synthase 3" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT4G02280-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="750" centerY="595" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The SUS3 sucrose synthase appears to play an important role in carbohydrate metabolism during seed maturation. Analyses of a sus3 mutant revealed a deficiency in sucrose synthase activity 18 days after flowering |CITS: [20559653]|. This is consistent with the observation that SUS3 transcript levels increase significantly during the late maturation stages of seed development |CITS:[18635527][18701523][20559653][17257168]|. sus3 mutant plants have decreased starch levels during certain periods of embryonic development as well as decreased fatty acid concentrations. Many other metabolic perturbations were also observed in sus3 mutants during seed maturation |CITS: [20559653]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT4G02280-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="AtSUS3" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="Sucrose-UDP glucosyltransferase 3" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33398, RXN-6039" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="2" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT4G02280.1" />
      <Property key="FunctionalAssignmentStatus" value=":PROBABLE-ENZYME" />
