    <DataNode elementId="AT5G49190-MONOMER" textLabel="Sucrose synthase 2" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="AT5G49190-MONOMER" dataSource="plantcyc" />
      <Graphics centerX="750" centerY="755" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The SUS2 sucrose synthase appears to play an important role in carbohydrate metabolism during seed maturation. Although efforts to directly assay for enzyme activity failed due to problems with enzyme solubility |CITS: [17257168]|, analyses of a sus2 mutant revealed a deficiency in sucrose synthase activity 12 and 15 days after flowering |CITS: [20559653]|. There are some reports that SUS2 transcript levels are increased in leaves specifically by O(2) deficiency |CITS: [10567234]| whereas other reports indicate that SUS2 is expressed only in seeds |CITS: [20559653]|. Further exploration of the expression pattern during seed development indicated that SUS2 transcript and protein levels peak about 15 days after flowering, consistent with the loss of sucrose synthase activity in the sus2 mutant during this time period |CITS: [18635527][18701523][20559653]|. sus2 mutant plants have decreased starch levels during certain periods of embryonic development as well as decreased fatty acid concentrations, but they also have elevated total protein levels from 12 to 15 days after flowering. Many other metabolic perturbations were also discerned during this period of seed maturation |CITS: [20559653]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT5G49190-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="AtSUS2" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="Sucrose-UDP glucosyltransferase 2" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33543, RXN-6884" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="2" />
      <Property key="GOTerms" value="GO:0005829, GO:0009536" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT5G49190.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT5G49190" />
      <Property key="^citations" value="18701523, 18701523" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <Property key="Locations" value="CCI-CYTOSOL-PL, CCO-PLASTID" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_17257168" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_20559653" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_10567234" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT2G35020-MONOMER" textLabel="UDP-N-acetylglucosamine diphosphorylase 2" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="O64765" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="900" centerY="755" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">UDP-N-acetylglucosamine (UDP-GlcNAc) is an essential precursor for glycoprotein and glycolipid biosynthesis in plants and it can also serve as a regulatory modification on signaling proteins. This enzyme, GlcNAc1pUT2, is capable of synthesizing |FRAME: UDP-N-ACETYL-D-GLUCOSAMINE| (UDP-GlcNAc) from |FRAME: UTP| and |FRAME: N-ACETYL-D-GLUCOSAMINE-1-P| &lt;i&gt;in vitro&lt;/i&gt; |CITS: [20557289]|. It can also catalyze the reverse reaction using |FRAME: UDP-N-ACETYL-D-GLUCOSAMINE UDP-GlcNAc| and the less common 4-epimer, |FRAME: UDP-N-ACETYL-GALACTOSAMINE| (UDP-GalNAc) |CITS: [20557289]|. In addition, unlike the related protein |FRAME: AT1G31070-MONOMER GlcNAc1pUT1|, this enzyme can also act on |FRAME: GLC-1-P|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G35020-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT2G35020.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Panther" value="PTHR11952" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pride" value="O64765" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Smr" value="O64765" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Pfam" value="PF01704" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Interpro" value="IPR029044" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="O64765" />
      <Property key="Synonym_1" value="N-acetylglucosamine-1-phosphate uridylyltransferase 2" />
      <Property key="Synonym_2" value="UDP-N-acetylgalactosamine diphosphorylase 2" />
      <Property key="Synonym_3" value="UTP--glucose-1-phosphate uridylyltransferase 2" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33739, RXN-33738, RXN-T9-2226, RXN-12846, RXN-12845" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="5" />
